WEBVTT

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:35.070
In the fourth round of the Summer Tournament,

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.700
we, Nishiura High, defeated Sakitama and advanced to the fifth round,

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:39.740
which would decide who got into the quarter-finals.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:44.330
Bijoudai Sayama defeated us, 11 to 6.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:48.830
But in two weeks, there's the Newcomers Game.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:51.250
We can't let ourselves stay depressed.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.590
For that purpose, Captain Hanai suggested

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:58.970
that we should talk about our team's goal.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:01.850
The team's goal.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.850
Abe — get to Koshien.

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:06.140
Chiyo — Koshien.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:10.020
Sakaeguchi — this year's Fall Tournament round of 16.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:12.070
Next year's Spring, round of 16.

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:15.190
Summer quarter-finals. Fall quarter-finals.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:18.110
The year after that, Spring finals, and Summer Championship.

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:21.070
Mizutani — win the Prefectural Tournament.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.870
Suyama — National Tournament.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.700
Nishihiro — get to the National Tournament.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.460
Oki — win the Prefectural Tournament.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:32.340
Izumi — get to Koshien.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.670
Hanai — Koshien.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:38.220
Mihashi — Koshien Championship.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:41.050
Tajima — best in the country.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:43.970
Um...

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.730
Nishihiro, can I count your National Tournament the same as quarter-finals for Koshien?

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.440
Yeah. Sorry for the confusion.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.900
Then in other words, everyone...

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:58.070
wants to go to Koshien, right?

00:02:58.070 --> 00:02:59.150
Yeah.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:02.620
And Tajima and Mihashi want to win Koshien?

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:03.490
Yeah!

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:07.790
You're going to change it?

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.710
Hey, we have to get to a common goal, right?

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.210
Yeah, that's the idea.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:18.460
Then what if we said,
"Get to Koshien or better?"

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.300
Everyone would...

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.510
No go, huh?

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:26.640
It's like the difference between aiming for 50% and 100%.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:28.810
Is it that different?

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:29.730
It is.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:34.190
Just look at the numbers: one out of 170 versus one out of 4,000.

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:36.190
That's really different.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.150
I want to turn back time three minutes.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.480
Even looking at the number of games...

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:39.240
No, that's not it.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.150
It's the difference between winning eight games and winning fourteen.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:42.200
The problem is that I wrote this goal with quite a lot of resolve.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.700
With that, saying 50% and 100% doesn't really capture it.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:45.450
Right?

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:47.740
Shit!

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:50.040
Let's all go with "Best in the country."

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:51.580
That's...

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:54.830
If we do that, to me,

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.960
it feels too unrealistic.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.920
If it wasn't unrealistic,
you couldn't call it a goal, right?

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.220
I don't think that's true.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:08.010
Or rather, if the goal seems impossible, it's the same as having no goal.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:08.760
It's different!

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:10.640
Because you're aiming for it, right?

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:12.520
Hanai.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.230
Why are we deciding on a goal?

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:20.480
For example, in middle school, our goal was to win the Prefectural Tournament,

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:24.780
so we made a big banner and put it on the back net.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.240
Is that what you meant by a goal?

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:30.080
It's fine to make something concrete out of it, but...

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.710
Changing our frame of mind might require something like that.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:33.750
Then, you know,

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.090
I feel it would be okay if everyone had different goals.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:42.880
I wrote this goal with all the conviction I had.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:45.380
This is my best...

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.850
and if everyone tries hard in their own way,

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:52.140
then isn't that the best the team can do?

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.480
We won't become the best in the country like that!

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.810
You... I told you that was unrealistic, didn't I?

00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:59.440
I know,

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:00.320
but if we don't aim for a goal...

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:01.900
This guy's serious?

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:03.650
You're contradicting what you said before.

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.360
Why is this..

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:08.070
I wanted to side with Tajima.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:13.790
Truthfully, I wanted to write down "Best in Japan" as well, but...

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:16.540
after that game, it's hard to say that.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:20.800
Then you think that winning Koshien is realistic, right, Tajima?

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:24.920
What were you thinking when you wrote that!?

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:29.220
That's right!

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:29.970
Mihashi also...

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.430
Mihashi also wrote, "Win Koshien."

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.390
If Mihashi would just speak to us...

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:37.310
I-I... I...

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.770
Just tell us what you're thinking.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:44.320
I... Nishihiro...

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:46.780
I...

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:54.080
What do I want to do with this team?

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:58.290
I want us to keep winning, and to stay together until the end.

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:04.380
But maybe that's not a goal.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:11.600
I... didn't really think about it.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.760
I-I'm sorry.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:15.810
Hanai.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:16.560
Yeah.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:17.770
Sorry.

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:23.020
I also didn't really think about it and just wrote down my childhood dream.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:26.610
I'll think it over properly, so can you give me until tomorrow to decide?

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:29.820
Oh, okay. I guess I did make you write it rather suddenly.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:30.360
Coach?

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:34.410
Yeah, that's fine. Let's do it again tomorrow.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:37.830
Incidentally, our practices now are pretty tough, but once we decide on our goal,

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:42.920
I'll put together a training regimen geared towards that.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:46.340
If you choose an ambitious goal,
be sure your resolve is equal to it.

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:46.800
Yes, ma'am!

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:48.470
Coach!

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:50.260
Coach, please tell us your goal.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:52.850
I want to win them all.

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:55.600
But <i>you</i> boys are the ones playing baseball.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:58.350
Today, with the end of the
Championship Tournament,

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:01.900
your high school baseball careers will last about another two years.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:05.570
Before tomorrow, please think carefully about how you want to spend those two years.

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:06.530
Yes, ma'am!

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:08.900
Ah, by the way...

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:12.990
Both Mr. Shiga and I have a PTA meeting, so go home at six.

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:14.990
Really?

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:16.450
Well, there's not much time, so next...

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:18.950
Let's reflect on today's game.

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:20.040
Okay.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:24.540
We lost in the end, but I don't think we have time to be depressed.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.460
Sorry for pressuring you.
Let's not leave thinking, "It was beyond us."

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:27.500
Let's discuss things that will help us next time.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:28.760
Pressuring?

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:29.760
Yeah!

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:32.890
It's past six!

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:34.470
Get moving!

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:35.430
Okay!

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:38.930
Mihashi.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:40.730
You've stopped in place.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.310
Are you so hungry that you can't move?

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:43.770
Th-That's not it!

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:46.820
Abe Takaya.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.280
Reply when you see this.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.030
I don't have to change right away.

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.650
Um, Mihashi.
I don't have to change right away.

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:53.110
Yes!?

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:56.410
I'm sorry. I read your mail.

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:56.950
Mail?

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.660
And you know, practice ended early today,

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:04.170
so why don't you go see Abe at his house?

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:06.840
Today might be your only chance to take the time and talk.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:09.090
But, his house...

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:10.460
I know where it is.

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:11.380
I'll draw you a map.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:21.890
You should go.

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:22.890
Yeah.

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:25.690
Abe is probably the most depressed today.

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:26.360
That's right.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:27.020
Depre-

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:28.110
He was injured and all.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:30.650
But I can understand why you're scared after getting this mail.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:33.150
You're wondering what he'll say to you.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.990
Plus this subject sounds really impatient.

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:41.120
Th-That's because I didn't reply, so...

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.120
Oh, really?

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:44.710
Can you find it with this map?

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:48.710
Take the industrial road and get off the outer ring at number 17.

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:49.710
Let me see.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.630
This is the co-op store and...

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:54.720
I'll go too.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:57.050
It's difficult if you don't have a feel for the area.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:58.050
I'll go too.

00:08:58.640 --> 00:08:59.970
Hurry up and get changed.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:01.060
Yeah.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:05.190
I'll reply that we're heading over now.

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:07.860
Why do you know where Abe lives?

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.020
Before I moved, I lived close by.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:13.650
Coach! We're out of mosquito-repellent sticks!

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:15.030
They were in the same middle school, after all.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:17.660
That's how it is, I guess. Yeah.

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:23.870
This is it.

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:35.550
Welcome!

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:37.510
Hello!

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:39.220
Abe's little brother?

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:40.180
Yes.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:43.560
Um, you're Arashii's Tajima, right?

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:44.020
Yeah.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:46.560
I'm with the Kawaguchi Eagles.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.150
Oh, the Eagles?

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.480
Arashii won the Kantou Tournament again this year, right?

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:50.940
Tajima's amazing.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:52.950
Please come inside!
Tajima's amazing.

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:52.980
Eagles?
Tajima's amazing.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:54.690
Eagles?

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:56.700
The Kawaguchi's Boys League team.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:58.820
N-Not the Senior?

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:00.950
Tajima was in Boys.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:03.370
Abe and I played Senior.

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:07.250
When you play in middle school, I guess you can't really tell the difference, huh?

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:08.170
Yeah.

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:13.630
Senior team names are all place names,
so teams like the Sea Breams are Boys League.

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:15.710
What would you guys like to drink?

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.050
What've you got?

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:17.800
Hey!

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:20.510
I'd thought that you knew a lot about Tajima,

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:22.140
but it's because your little brother was in the Boys League, right?

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:23.470
Yeah.

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:27.600
When we were kids, my parents said that brothers shouldn't play on the same team.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:29.810
Feel free to use the cushions.

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:32.150
Is this the living room?

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:34.780
Somehow, it sort of feels really formal.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:36.360
I didn't bring a present either.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:39.700
My room's on the second floor,
and using the stairs is hard,

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.660
so I'm staying here while I'm recuperating.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:43.370
I see. It's your knee after all.

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:45.330
No. The nurse said so.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:46.700
Oh, okay.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:48.160
That's right. Your knee!

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:51.920
Tajima. Don't wander around so much in someone else's house.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:53.880
Can you make the Newcomers Game?

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.510
I'll just barely be ready.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:58.380
Really?

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:01.430
Today was really tough for me, you know.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:02.090
Sorry.

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:03.350
You don't have to apologize.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.560
It's not like you wanted to get injured.

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:08.020
I also caused trouble during the Sakitama game.

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:10.770
But we get injured when we're careless.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.190
Let's both be careful!

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:12.770
Yeah.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:15.480
But you have a second-degree sprain, right?

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:17.230
Isn't two weeks pushing it?

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:22.200
When my friend got a second-degree ankle sprain, he couldn't play for two months.

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:25.240
T-Two months.

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:26.870
What did Coach Momo say?

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:29.160
Just barely. She said the same thing.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:33.130
But if you don't let a sprain heal properly, it'll happen again, right?

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:38.340
If your recovery was delayed, and you couldn't come to winter training, it'd be really bad.

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:41.130
Today was tough for me.

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:44.850
I hadn't prepared beforehand and couldn't keep up mentally.

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:47.220
I couldn't concentrate when hitting.

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:48.600
I'm the clean-up hitter, right?

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:51.230
There are things I want to do batting clean-up.

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:54.860
I couldn't do them, and that was tough!

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.820
I-I see.

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:58.320
That's true.

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:00.740
That's why I want to be mentally prepared next time.

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:04.360
I'll be catching in the Newcomers Game,

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:06.910
and maybe even the Fall Tournament as well.

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:08.080
So be sure to let it heal properly!

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:13.540
Sorry to intrude!

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:16.330
What would everyone like for dinner?

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:19.750
I'll be heading back now.

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:22.510
My little brother's home alone.

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:24.760
Crap, what time is it?

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:27.720
It's past seven!

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:31.020
Abe, I also... Here we go...

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:34.270
I also think that it won't take you long to heal completely.

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:36.270
Yeah. Thanks for coming today.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:38.270
Take care! Later!

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:40.230
Good work today! See you tomorrow.

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:41.690
Good work!

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:46.160
Kazuya's katsudon is delicious.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:48.030
All right! Then I'm getting katsudon.

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:48.410
Me too!

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:50.240
A soba store?

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:52.750
I'll have a katsudon, pork stew, and eel.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:53.910
That much?

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:56.710
I need nutrients to recover from my injury.

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:58.880
Until I'm better, I'll eat as much as I can.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:01.130
But are you sure about all three!?

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:03.340
Huh?

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:10.600
You can't rush it, but I'll be cheering for you to heal quickly.

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:12.060
I know that.

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:12.810
Ah, really?

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:14.940
Well, excuse me.

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:16.520
Tajima!

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:19.730
Before the food comes,
will you take a look at my swing?

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:20.770
Yeah, sure.

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:24.110
Why don't I teach you the Arashii swing!

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:26.360
All right! I'll go get a bat.

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:27.200
Okay.

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:29.160
Do you have two bats?

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:30.990
Yes!

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:32.660
Mihashi, what will you have?

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:39.580
Ka... Por... Eel...

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:42.420
What are you going to eat!?

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:45.170
Katsu... Eel...

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:50.680
A fierce heat wave starts next week.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:54.430
Now, moving on, here's tomorrow's weather.

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:56.100
Partly cloudy. Some places may feel uncomfortably humid.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:57.270
Por...

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:58.060
Partly cloudy. Some places may feel uncomfortably humid.

00:13:58.060 --> 00:13:58.940
Eel...

00:13:58.940 --> 00:13:59.650
Watch out for sudden heavy showers. Chance of rain is 40%.

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:01.860
K-Katsu...

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:02.650
Watch out for sudden heavy showers. Chance of rain is 40%.

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:03.980
Katsudon and eel, right!?

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:05.610
K-Katsudon!

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:12.580
I'm going to try hard. I have to speak my mind.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.040
Now, next is high school baseball.

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:19.250
Today, the representatives from Kagoshima and Iwata prefectures were decided.

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.630
Yes, thank you.

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:29.220
Today's results are in the newspaper.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:33.390
Fast.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:34.850
Because it's the evening paper.

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:36.470
O-Oh.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:40.850
We lost.

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:45.650
Yeah.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:51.280
The mail...

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:55.120
S-Sorry for not replying!

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:56.580
Forget about the subject line.

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:57.870
About the contents...

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:01.080
Um, I-I also have something to say.

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:01.790
Something?

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:03.380
Yes!

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:03.920
What?

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:08.800
I'll start first.

00:15:13.340 --> 00:15:16.060
I broke my promise. I'm sorry!

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:23.610
I said that I wouldn't get sick or injured,
and that I'd catch for all your games, right?

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:27.900
Th-That's because I'm pathetic, so it was reassuring.

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:28.820
I know that!

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:33.700
Still, I was happy that you were more confident...

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:37.120
when I was the catcher.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:40.460
Getting injured and having to leave mid-game...

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:43.580
It really bothered me, so let me apologize!

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:44.670
I'm sorry!

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:46.130
O-Okay.

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:51.300
Also, when we first met, I'm sorry for telling you not to shake me off.

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:54.180
That was a mistake.

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:56.140
I'm sorry.

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.940
I wanted to talk about that too.

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:04.230
Um...

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:08.780
Today, I shook off some signs.

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:14.360
And then, it seemed like I was consulting with Tajima.

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:18.490
Tajima relied on me. Isn't that amazing!?

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:21.120
Yeah. It is.

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:25.040
I've...

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:29.090
I've just relied on you until now, Abe.

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:32.510
I'll...

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:34.680
I'll work hard, so...

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:39.890
Rely on me, Abe!

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:44.350
Okay.

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:47.440
Let's combine our strengths and become strong!

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:54.240
Yeah!

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:55.860
He smiled.

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:57.200
That's right.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:59.200
That's the first time I've seen it.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:07.660
Why did I think he was like Haruna?

00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:09.920
I don't need any signs.

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:12.130
Besides, only half go where I'm aiming.

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:15.010
You wouldn't understand the impatience someone feels

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:17.300
after getting injured unless you too were hurt.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:20.640
Getting injured and then sidelined...

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:27.520
Even after recovering, being sidelined again...

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:34.110
Got it!

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:40.620
Here. The team meeting and goal.

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:41.910
Oh, let me see.

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:46.710
You put Koshien Championship!? Talk about big!

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:53.380
The team is going to pick one goal, so we're meeting again tomorrow.

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:56.340
All right then. What did coach say?

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:59.260
C-Coach said to be prepared.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:01.350
Once we decide on a goal, she'll be training us hard.

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:04.140
His memory and playback are also jerky.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:08.020
And lastly, coach said that she wanted to win everything.

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:14.110
During the Spring Tournament, let's go see Urawashie.

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:15.900
H-Haruna.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:16.990
That's right.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:22.830
Back then, Coach Momo said that an overly ambitious goal isn't really a goal.

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:27.290
At the time, I thought,
"Well, I guess that's how it is,"

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:32.170
but actually, almost everyone was preoccupied just thinking about the quarter-finals.

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:38.670
It means that Coach Momo, Tajima, and you are all idiots, in a good sense.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.930
All right. I'll make mine Koshien Championship too.

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:45.060
A hard practice is just what I want right now.

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:49.060
Well, it still doesn't seem quite real,

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:52.060
but if the coach, Tajima, and you are aiming for that,

00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:54.020
then I want to be part of it!

00:18:56.980 --> 00:18:58.570
Food's here!

00:18:58.570 --> 00:18:59.650
Let's eat!

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:01.410
All right!

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:06.490
Let's eat!

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:08.790
Looks good!

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:10.290
Good!

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:16.500
Tender.

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:18.630
Thanks for the meal!

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:20.010
That was delicious!

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:22.050
Well then, take care of yourself!

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:24.140
Th-Thanks for the food.

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:28.680
Tajima, thank you very much!

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:30.810
Sure. Work hard.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:33.150
You, too. Thanks.

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:35.730
Um, t-take care.

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:38.360
I'll be going to the training camp,
so I'll see you there.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:39.190
Yeah.

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:43.070
Later!

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:44.700
Goodbye!

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:49.620
Hey! Who was the other person with Tajima?

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:50.830
Mihashi?

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:52.080
The pitcher?

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:56.460
He had a nice smile. I liked him.

00:19:58.630 --> 00:19:59.130
What?

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:02.130
You wouldn't know...

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:04.390
Why?

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:16.480
Tajima, do you know the way?

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:17.570
No problem.

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:21.280
Mail!

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:24.860
It's Shuu!

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:28.240
Who?

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:29.830
K-Kanou.

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:30.950
From Mihoshi Academy?

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:34.920
We lost to Maebashi Eitoku.

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:38.670
Even though we were only three games away from Koshien...

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:45.300
Starting now, our goal is to win next summer's Koshien.

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:01.440
Tajima.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:07.700
A rival! How nice, Mihashi.

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:15.580
You're not pressuring me.

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:19.630
My goal is...

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:23.630
best in the country!

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:27.470
Right!?

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:28.550
Yeah!

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:45.440
We have to make it the team's goal, not just ours.

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:04.550
Because if everyone doesn't aim for it together, we won't be able to do it!
